MultiCue's audio engine is a deliberate C++ port of the spatial-audio and
loudness algorithms in:

  MultichannelPlayer
  https://github.com/alib65/MultichannelPlayer
  Copyright (c) 2026 Ali Balighi
  MIT License

MultichannelPlayer is a SuperCollider playlist player for multichannel music
made from separate mono files. Its layout presets, spherical-harmonics
Ambisonic encoding/decoding (ACN/SN3D, AllRAD, max-rE), VBAP panning with
imaginary speakers, constant-power stereo downmix, FuMa/AmbiX conversion, and
EBU R128 / ITU-R BS.1770 loudness analysis are ported into mc_dsp and
mc_engine; see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 0 for the full function-by-
function mapping. Thank you to Ali Balighi for releasing the original work
under the MIT license, which made this port possible.

